<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sugar Ray Robinson returns six weeks after intake with his care partner, whom he asked to be present. The amyloid PET two weeks ago was positive. He was asked first how much he wanted to know and said he wanted it straight. The diagnosis of Alzheimer&apos;s disease at the stage of mild dementia was explained with the PET, MRI and test results, in plain words and in writing. He was quiet, then asked whether boxing had caused it; that question was answered honestly. His home glucose readings ran 95 to 150 mg/dL, with one reading of 68 mg/dL before lunch on glipizide. He has not driven. His care partner finds the evenings and the repeated questions tiring. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Amyloid PET</td><td>Positive, widespread cortical uptake</td></tr><tr><td>Diagnosis</td><td>Mild dementia due to Alzheimer&apos;s disease, early onset</td></tr><tr><td>Home glucose</td><td>95 to 150 mg/dL; one reading of 68 mg/dL on glipizide</td></tr><tr><td>ECG</td><td>Sinus rhythm 70, normal intervals</td></tr><tr><td>Care partner</td><td>Zarit Burden Interview 18 (mild), narrative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

