<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alzheimer&apos;s disease with early onset (G30.0)</content>. Amyloid PET positive: the amnestic mild dementia is due to Alzheimer&apos;s disease, beginning before 65. Repetitive head impacts may have added to his difficulty, and traumatic encephalopathy syndrome remains a research diagnosis that cannot be confirmed in life; it would not change his treatment. He is not a candidate for anti-amyloid antibodies because of the microbleeds. Donepezil offered for modest benefit and accepted after a normal ECG. [S]<list><item>Donepezil 5 mg at bedtime; raise to 10 mg after four to six weeks if tolerated.</item><item>MoCA and CDR yearly, or sooner with change.</item><item>Exercise and social activity to continue.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Mild dementia due to Alzheimer&apos;s disease (F02.A0)</content>. CDR 1. Getting lost while driving and the CDR put him at high risk at the wheel; after discussion he agreed to stop driving. He agreed to have the handgun taken out of the home. [S]<list><item>No driving; transport through his care partner and paratransit.</item><item>Handgun removed from the home.</item><item>Care partner: Alzheimer&apos;s Association 24/7 Helpline, a caregiver class, and an adult day program two days a week for respite.</item><item>GUIDE dementia care program once he has Medicare.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Type 2 diabetes (E11.9)</content>. A low reading of 68 mg/dL on glipizide with hemoglobin A1c 6.4%: under the ADA Standards for an older adult with cognitive impairment, the goal is under 8.0% and sulfonylureas should be stopped to avoid hypoglycemia. [S]<list><item>Stop glipizide.</item><item>Continue metformin; hold it on days he cannot eat or drink.</item><item>Hemoglobin A1c at about three months.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Bilateral sensorineural hearing loss (H90.3)</content>. Hearing aids recommended by the audiologist. [S]<list><item>Hearing aid fitting in two weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive testing (MoCA, MMSE)</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly, or sooner with change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MoCA 18 and MMSE 22 at diagnosis; next in a year</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Dementia staging (CDR) and function (ADL and IADL)</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>CDR 1 two weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Amyloid biomarker confirmation (PET or CSF)</td><td>Once, when it will change diagnosis or treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Amyloid PET positive (about 90 Centiloids), reviewed with him today</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Anti-amyloid antibody eligibility (lecanemab, donanemab), APOE genotyping and ARIA MRI schedule</td><td>At diagnosis of MCI or mild dementia due to Alzheimer&apos;s disease</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not a candidate because of six microbleeds; explained to him today</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medicine review for anticholinergic and sedating drugs (Beers)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No anticholinergic or sedating drugs; glipizide stopped for hypoglycemia risk</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Behavioral and psychological symptoms (NPI-Q items)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None; sad at the news without depression</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Cholinesterase inhibitor: benefit, nausea, diarrhea, dreams, pulse</td><td>Each follow-up and each dose change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Donepezil 5 mg started after a normal ECG (pulse 70)</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Driving, firearm and home safety</td><td>At diagnosis and each follow-up</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Agreed to stop driving; handgun to be removed from the home; stove shut-off advised</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Care partner support and burden (Zarit, narrative)</td><td>At diagnosis, then at least yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Zarit 18 (mild burden); helpline, caregiver class and adult day program arranged; GUIDE explained for when he has Medicare</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning</td><td>At diagnosis; revisit yearly and at changes</td><td>Due</td><td>Booked at the preventive visit in three weeks, while he can take part fully</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin A1c, goal under 8.0% for an older adult with cognitive impairment, and hypoglycemia review</td><td>Every three months after a therapy change; every six months when stable</td><td>Up to date</td><td>6.4% at intake; one low reading; glipizide stopped; A1c due in about three months</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure, goal under 130/80 mmHg</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>126/78 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Potassium and creatinine on lisinopril and metformin</td><td>Yearly, and after acute illness or dehydration</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Dilated diabetic eye examination</td><td>Every one to two years without retinopathy</td><td>Referred</td><td>Still pending; he now depends on others for transport</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise and social activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Walks daily; the foundation gym twice a week</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Find the cause of the memory loss and explain it to him in a way he can take in. Outcome by 2026-08-18: Alzheimer&apos;s disease confirmed by amyloid PET; disclosed with his care partner present, at his request, with written notes [S]</item><item>No hypoglycemia, with hemoglobin A1c under 8.0%. In progress; target